From: Qianhui Xu <xiaqinghuan@mail.ustc.edu.cn>
Subject: [PATCH] osk-stub: keep self-composing completers (Rime) active on every keystroke

---
The 0.46 completion modes are 'none', 'manual' and 'hint'.
'hint' enables completion only when the client advertises
ZWP_TEXT_INPUT_V3_CONTENT_HINT_COMPLETION, which e.g. the Firefox URL bar
never does, so a completer that composes by itself (the Rime completer)
never receives any keystroke and can't offer candidates.

Treat such completers as always active. No new gsettings value is needed
(adding an enum value would need a compatible compiled schema) and the
behaviour of the bundled hunspell/presage completers is unchanged.
---
--- a/src/pos-input-surface.c
+++ b/src/pos-input-surface.c
@@ -2012,6 +2012,23 @@
   return self->screen_keyboard_enabled;
 }
 
+/* Completers that do the composition themselves (e.g. Rime) cannot rely on the
+   client advertising ZWP_TEXT_INPUT_V3_CONTENT_HINT_COMPLETION - many clients
+   (Firefox's URL bar among them) never set that hint.  Keep such completers
+   active on every keystroke so they can drive their own preedit. */
+static gboolean
+completer_composes_by_itself (PosCompleter *completer)
+{
+  const char *name;
+
+  if (completer == NULL)
+    return FALSE;
+
+  name = pos_completer_get_name (completer);
+
+  return g_strcmp0 (name, "Rime") == 0;
+}
+
 gboolean
 pos_input_surface_is_completer_active (PosInputSurface *self)
 {
@@ -2025,6 +2042,9 @@
   if (pos_input_method_get_active (self->input_method) == FALSE)
     return FALSE;
 
+  if (completer_composes_by_itself (self->completer))
+    return TRUE;
+
   /* Layout has an "implicit" completer (e.g. varnam) */
   child = hdy_deck_get_visible_child (self->deck);
   if (POS_IS_OSK_WIDGET (child) &&
